# Week 4 tests (Express + PostgreSQL)
# 1) Run database.sql in pgAdmin  2) npm start  3) run from top to bottom

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001

### 1. Database health (200, database time)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/database

### 2. Get all movies (200, array from PostgreSQL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies

### 3. Get an existing movie (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### 4. Get a missing movie (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/999

### 5. Invalid id (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/abc

### 6. Create a valid movie (201, PostgreSQL creates the id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Arrival",
  "director": "Denis Villeneuve",
  "year": 2016
}

### 7. Create an invalid movie (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "year": "not a number"
}

### 8. Replace a movie with PUT (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Inception: Updated Edition",
  "director": "Christopher Nolan",
  "year": 2010
}

### 9. Incomplete PUT (400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Inception"
}

### 10. PATCH one field (200, only year changes)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "year": 2011
}

### 11. Empty PATCH (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 12. Filter by director (200, case-insensitive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?director=nolan

### 13. Filter by year and sort by year (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?minYear=2000&sortBy=year

### 14. Sort by title (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?sortBy=title

### 15. Invalid sortBy (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?sortBy=rating

### 16. Delete a movie (204, no body)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/2

### 17. Delete the same movie again (404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/2

### 18. Persistence test: create a movie, then restart Express and run #2 again
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Dune",
  "director": "Denis Villeneuve",
  "year": 2021
}
